 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
AB ⟂ AC [00]
A,B,D are collinear [01]
DA = DB [02]
A,E,C are collinear [03]
EA = EC [04]
DF = DA [05]
F,B,C are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. DF = DA [05] & DA = DB [02] ⇒  DB = DF [07]
002. DB = DF [07] ⇒  ∠DBF = ∠BFD [08]
003. A,B,D are collinear [01] & DA = DB [02] ⇒  D is midpoint of AB [09]
004. A,E,C are collinear [03] & EA = EC [04] ⇒  E is midpoint of AC [10]
005. D is midpoint of AB [09] & E is midpoint of AC [10] ⇒  DE ∥ BC [11]
006. A,B,D are collinear [01] & ∠DBF = ∠BFD [08] & F,B,C are collinear [06] & BC ∥ DE [11] ⇒  ∠ADE = ∠EDF [12]
007. DF = DA [05] & ∠ADE = ∠EDF [12] (SAS)⇒  ∠DAE = ∠EFD [13]
008. ∠DAE = ∠EFD [13] & A,B,D are collinear [01] & A,E,C are collinear [03] & AB ⟂ AC [00] ⇒  DF ⟂ FE
